menu "Knob time (K7d SNTP)"

config KNOB_NTP_SERVER
    string "NTP server hostname"
    default "pool.ntp.org"
    help
        The single POLL server (same default the clock's
        CLOCK_NTP_SERVER uses). The credentials WLAN must have an
        uplink; without one the display honestly reads "no time".

config KNOB_TIME_BOOT_SYNC_MS
    int "Boot NTP fix window (ms)"
    default 20000
    range 5000 120000
    help
        How long the boot arm task waits for the first plausible SNTP
        answer before giving up on the sweep window (lwIP adds up to
        CONFIG_LWIP_SNTP_MAXIMUM_STARTUP_DELAY before its first
        request). After the window the glass stays "no time" and a
        late fix arms the STATIC current phase instead of a sweep.

config KNOB_TIME_USE_TEST_EPOCH
    bool "Bench: frozen KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH as now (no SNTP)"
    default n
    help
        Bench builds only: the boot arm treats KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH as
        a trusted instant and never starts SNTP -- this is what keeps
        the K7b/K7c frozen-epoch verifications (blood tint at the
        2025-03-14 eclipse, the single midnight re-bake) reproducible.
        Production leaves this n: SNTP truth or "no time".

endmenu
